      "block": "原句1",
      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Zak relaxed back here because Dale was comfortable in the store and loved to busy himself with rearranging things to “gi",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 526
        }
      ],
      "words": 24
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Zara hates that I lie and say Mom’s at an estate sale or whatever, but I don’t see the point in upsetting him",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1847
        }
      ],
      "words": 23
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "But we own the building. The rentals upstairs and the shop next door give us enough to keep the lights on",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2013
        }
      ],
      "words": 21
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I’m not your son, Meg. You don’t have to solve my problems for me",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3377
        }
      ],
      "words": 14
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I wasn’t going to say it because it sounds like I’m only saying it to keep you here, but I do. Now you know",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4182
        }
      ],
      "words": 24
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
